  "term": "cerebrovascular accident",
  "definition": "A cerebrovascular accident, or stroke, is a sudden loss of neurological function caused by reduced blood flow to the brain or bleeding inside the skull. It refers to a group of conditions that vary by the type and location of brain tissue damage and by whether bleeding is involved.",
